message: "Please cite this release and, separately, the upstream datasets listed under references. Version 1.1.0 is DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23770989; version 1.0.0 is DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23401265."
type: software
title: "HelmX: Reproducibility Package for Deployment-Fidelity Validation of a Helmet-Mounted IMU Event-Detection Policy on Raspberry Pi 4"
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-02"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23770989"
authors:
  - family-names: "Azfar"
    given-names: "Usman"
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Science, Faculty of Computing and Information Technology, University of the Punjab, Lahore, Pakistan"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Usman-Azfar/HelmX-AI-Powered-Smart-Helmet/tree/crash-detection"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.23770989"
    description: "Version 1.1.0 of this reproducibility package"
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.23401265"
    description: "Version 1.0.0 (previous version of this package)"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: "Reproducibility and evidence package for deployment-fidelity validation of a helmet-mounted IMU crash-detection policy on Raspberry Pi 4: frozen code, the deployed INT8 detector and thresholds, curated offline and external-validation results, and Raspberry Pi validation evidence. Version 1.1.0 adds offline studies (three simple baseline detectors under the same validation protocol, an isolated analysis of the training/runtime jerk-feature discrepancy, and session-clustered bootstrap intervals) and corrects the dataset provenance: the road training sessions are a subset of the public STRIDE car-smartphone dataset, and the fall and near-fall sessions come from Boubezoul et al. The frozen model was not retrained. Licences are mixed (MIT for software, CC BY 4.0 for Raspberry Pi evidence, a redistribution notice for model artifacts, which are distributed only in the Zenodo archive); see DATA_LICENSES.md. Source datasets retain their own licences and are not included."
keywords:
  - crash detection
  - inertial sensors
  - Raspberry Pi
  - TensorFlow Lite
  - deployment validation
